The most important things to remember are:

1️⃣ useState

Stores changing information.

const [value, setValue] = useState();
2️⃣ useEffect

Synchronizes with external systems.

useEffect(() => {
  // effect
}, []);
3️⃣ Dependencies
[count]

means:

Re-run when count changes.

4️⃣ Cleanup
return () => {
  // cleanup
};

means:

Clean up what the effect created.

5️⃣ Don't overuse effects

If something can simply be calculated during rendering, you usually don't need an effect.

